id: pm-urzubi
title: "Starting work ignores open blockers: claim <id> --start and update --status in_progress move a blocked item into progress without a refusal or warning"
description: "Raised by CodeRabbit on PR #1645 and verified on 2026.10.31 source in a fresh sandbox. An item created with --blocked-by <open item> is stored as status blocked, and pm update <id> --status in_progress then succeeds with no refusal or warning. pm claim <id> --start runs the same claim-then-update composition, so it behaves the same. pm validate later reports non_blocked_status_has_blocked_by for the in-progress item whose blocker is still open. pm next and claim --next --start are unaffected because ready selection already excludes items with open blockers. Starting an explicitly blocked item is a governance decision, not a claim defect, so changing only --start would make start and update disagree.\n\nDuplicate search: 'start blocked item open blocker in_progress refuse', 'non_blocked_status_has_blocked_by' — no open item. Nearest is the dependency-aware actionability decision (closed)."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[4]: agent-ux,dependencies,governance,lifecycle
created_at: "2026-10-31T23:01:47.892Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-02T16:35:50.225Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-02T14:26:36.511Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-02T14:26:36.511Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: "Moving an item with an open blocked_by target into the in-progress status, through update, claim --start or start-task, either refuses with a typed code naming the open blocker and the unblock or --force recovery, or warns, as governed by a declared setting; the CLI, MCP and SDK paths share one check that runs before any write, so a refused start never leaves a claim; a terminal blocker does not block; tests cover refuse, warn and terminal-blocker cases"
parent: pm-33cw
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "sdk/lifecycle/start-blockers.ts admits or refuses a move into progress against currently open declared blockers, resolved through sdk/query/declared-blockers.ts (shared with the pm get blockers facet). update --status, claim --start, claim --next --start and start-task share it. Update and claim run it under the item lock; the explicit start composition pre-checks before the claim write. strict (default) refuses start_blocked_by_open_dependency with open_blockers details and an executable unblock command; --force overrides; warn and off are declared modes."
expected_result: No transport can silently move an item with an open blocker into progress; the behaviour is declared by governance settings and consistent across update and start.
actual_result: "Verified in specs and against the built CLI: update/claim --start/start-task refuse with exit 4 and leave no claim. The same-call unblock+start, terminal blockers and already-in-progress items are admitted. --force records start_blocker_override, warn records start_with_open_blockers, off is silent. The published 2026.11.2 negative control starts the blocked item silently."
